  "details": "VRCSDK3-2019.12.21.16.01\nUDONSDK-2019.12.22.12.32_Public\nVRChat build 893\nI noticed that sitting in a world where an error is occurring inside the update loop can result in a large amount of output log spam, which in turn increases the output log file size. (as demonstrated with my 1.11GB output log file)\nSide note: This can also occur in the unity editor as it logs everything as well.\nThe main concern here is that just Udon itself throwing a single error will spam logs without the user knowing. Resulting in some outrageous output log file sizes and what I presume to be constant writing to the drive.\nAs a quick experiment to see if this was possible to be malicious with, I was able to create a world with a single Udon graph that silently produces roughly 10MB of log spam a second. Also if you don't want a silent approach you can easily get upwards of 40MB a second but that is more likely to be noticed by the player as performance hitching.\nAn appropriate fix might be to throw an error then disable the offending script. If that breaks other Udon scripts they can just follow suit as the first error is what anyone debugging should look at.\nAn alternate fix idea might be to give the client the ability to enable Udon logging so that only creators should turn it on when they are debugging their worlds in game. That would avoid the average user from getting hit with this issue.",
